{"id":"H3866","lemma":"לוּדִי","transliteration":"ludi","sayIt":"lu-di","language":"Hebrew","partOfSpeech":"","gloss":"Ludite","meaning":"Someone descended from Egypt (H4714), first mentioned at Gen.10.13; along with Anamim (H6047), Lehabim (H3853), Naphtuhim (H5320), Pathrusim (H6625), Casluhim (H3695) and Caphtorim (H3732)\n§ Ludim or Lydians = \"to the firebrands: travailings\"\nthe descendants of Lud the son of Shem","glosses":["ludites","men of lydia"],"count":3,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"gen-10","v":13,"renderings":{"bsb":"the Ludites","kjv":"Ludim"}},{"chapterId":"1ch-1","v":11,"renderings":{"bsb":"the Ludites","kjv":"Ludim"}},{"chapterId":"jer-46","v":9,"renderings":{"bsb":"men of Lydia","kjv":"and the Lydians"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Genesis 10:13","note":"Mizraim became the father of Ludim, Anamim, Lehabim, Naphtuhim,","source":"web"},{"ref":"1 Chronicles 1:11","note":"Mizraim became the father of Ludim, Anamim, Lehabim, Naphtuhim,","source":"web"},{"ref":"Jeremiah 46:9","note":"Go up, you horses! Rage, you chariots! Let the mighty men go out: Cush and Put, who handle the shield; and the Ludim, who handle and bend the bow.","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"H3865","lemma":"לוּד","transliteration":"lud","gloss":"Lud"},{"id":"H3695","lemma":"כַּסְלֻחִים","transliteration":"kasluchim","gloss":"Casluhim"},{"id":"H3732","lemma":"כַּפְתֹּרִי","transliteration":"kaphtori","gloss":"Caphtorim"},{"id":"H3853","lemma":"לְהָבִים","transliteration":"lehavim","gloss":"Lehabim"},{"id":"H4714","lemma":"מִצְרַ֫יִם","transliteration":"mitsrayim","gloss":"Egypt"},{"id":"H6047","lemma":"עֲנָמִים","transliteration":"anamim","gloss":"Anamim"},{"id":"H5320","lemma":"נַפְתֻּחִים","transliteration":"naphtuchim","gloss":"Naphtuhim"},{"id":"H6625","lemma":"פַּתְרֻסִים","transliteration":"patrusi","gloss":"Pathrusim"}],"senses":[{"id":"H3866H","gloss":"Lydian","relation":"H3866H = a group of"}],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged te